\section*{Limitations}

Our primary experiments use ALFWorld with cross-environment validation on ScienceWorld. The theoretical argument is environment-agnostic, but additional environments would strengthen generality. The 8B experiments confirm the mechanisms extend across the two scales tested but report single-seed runs due to FSDP computational constraints. For very long episodes ($T > 100$) or tasks with many independent sub-goals, uniform episode-level advantage may limit efficiency even though it preserves direction correctness.

